# Issue #42: Prototype pollution vulnerability in deepExtend

**Reporter**: Calling `deepExtend({}, JSON.parse(userInput))` allows `__proto__` injection.

**Maintainer**: Note that v0.4.x is end-of-life and no upstream version will be released. You can safely mitigate this in application code by checking object keys before invoking deepExtend:

```javascript
function safeExtend(target, source) {
  for (const key of Object.keys(source)) {
    if (key === '__proto__' || key === 'constructor') {
      delete source[key];
    }
  }
  return deepExtend(target, source);
}
```

